  "lidar_note": "Task F (user decision 2026-10-11, option B): the LD14 is turned 180 deg about its spin axis (motor toward the back), spin axis x 54: the most forward position at which its 0.1 m minimum range (LD14P) stays inside the bumper skin with a half pressed to its stop, so the scan sees whatever the bumper touches (a trial at x 109, its front 10 mm inside the skin, left a 5 cm blind strip ahead of the bumper). Its 0 deg (tail/motor) direction points along robot -x: a driver scan angle theta (REP-103, CCW, 0 = LD14 tail) maps to the robot-frame bearing wrap(theta + 180 deg) into (-180, 180]; a raw LD14 angle a (clockwise from the tail) maps to wrap(180 deg - a). The simulator reports scans in the robot frame already. Task L (LIO-120, user request 2026-10-12): the LD14 sits 20 mm lower than in task F, laser plane 127.5 mm (was 147.5): the scan band (plane \u00b1 4 mm) is then exactly 20 mm over the lid top, the floor the scan-band rule allows. Its lugs sit straight on the tray plate (no towers); its motor drops into the tray's fan intake duct, 1.4 mm over the fan frame.",
