  "camera_led_note": "Task N (LIO-134): one Samsung LM281B+ Pro 2835 LED (5000 K, 37.5 lm at 65 mA / 2.7 V, 120 deg) above the lens, facing forward, its emitting face at x 145.8, z 89.45. From J15 pin 5 (5 V) through 39 ohm: (5 - 2.7) / 39 = 59 mA, so ~37.5 x 59 / 65 = 34 lm and ~34 / pi = 10.8 cd on axis (a near-Lambertian emitter). Switched low-side by a TN0702N3-G MOSFET from GP20 (J15 pin 3).",
  "camera_x_note": "camera_x = lens front face; the image frustum apex used for every clearance check is 3 mm behind it (x 143), the assumed worst entrance-pupil position; the lens solid centre is x 141.4. Task F: the camera sits in the bumper band behind a window in the two bumper halves (level, axis z 80). Below 80 mm the simulator camera loses the 6 cm shower tray in Unreal (straight drives at it: found in 6/10 at 75 mm, 10/10 at 80 mm); 80 is also the highest axis whose image still fits a window closed under the 98.5 mm bumper top.",
  "camera_image_note": "The simulator renders 640 \u00d7 360 (16:9, as the OV2735 1920 \u00d7 1080 mode); the CAD clearance check deliberately uses a taller 4:3 frustum (VFOV 68.06 deg), which is conservative.",
